# CLAUDE.md: <CHANNEL NAME>

<!--
How to use: copy this file to the root of your channel project folder as
CLAUDE.md, replace every <...> placeholder, and delete lines that do not apply.
Claude Code reads this file at the start of every session in that folder.
Keep it short and specific: rules Claude can follow, not wishes.
-->

## 1. Channel promise
- One sentence a viewer would repeat: "<This channel explains WHY ___ happens, in under 12 minutes, with sources.>"
- Every video must keep this promise. If a topic does not fit, say so.

## 2. Niche and audience
- Niche: <e.g. space science for curious adults, no jargon>
- Primary audience: <age range, interests, what they already know>
- Main countries / language: <e.g. United States, United Kingdom; English>
- What they watch instead of us: <2 to 3 competitor channels>

## 3. Voice and style rules
- Tone: <calm, curious, slightly dry humour>
- Reading level: <explain like a smart 15-year-old>
- Script length: <1,400 to 1,800 words for 10 to 12 minutes>
- Always: <hook with a question in the first 15 seconds; one idea per section>
- Never: <clickbait words like "SHOCKING"; fake urgency; filler intros>
- Spelling: <US / UK English>

## 4. What Claude may do
- Research topics with the `topic-research` skill and fill the decision sheet.
- Draft outlines, scripts, descriptions, chapters, captions and upload packs.
- Run the `pre-upload-qc` skill and local, read-only measurement tools.
- Organise files inside this project folder.

## 5. What Claude may not do
- Publish, upload, schedule or delete anything on YouTube or social accounts.
- Log in to accounts other than: <list approved accounts, or "none">.
- Spend money or use paid credits without asking first.
- Invent facts, quotes, statistics or sources.
- Copy another creator's script, structure or thumbnail.

## 6. Decisions only the owner makes
- Topic (Claude proposes, owner approves)
- Final title
- Thumbnail
- Publish date and time
- <anything else, e.g. sponsorships, music choice>

## 7. File and folder layout
```
<channel>/
  CLAUDE.md
  01_ideas/           decision sheets, one per topic
  02_scripts/         <NN>_<slug>_script_v<N>.md
  03_assets/          images, footage, music + credits.txt
  04_renders/         final exports
  05_upload/          <NN>_<slug>_upload-pack.txt, captions .srt
  06_analytics/       notes after publishing
```
- File naming: <NN>_<short-slug>, lowercase, hyphens, no spaces.

## 8. Quality bar
- Final render: <3840x2160 / 1920x1080>, <24/30> fps, <10 to 12> minutes.
- Audio: about -14 LUFS integrated, true peak at or below -1 dBTP.
- Captions on every video, checked against the final cut.
- Nothing ships without a full `pre-upload-qc` report marked "Ready: YES".

## 9. Sources policy
- Primary sources only for facts: <e.g. NASA, ESA, peer-reviewed papers, official statistics>.
- Every claim in the script gets a source link in the notes.
- Label certainty: Confirmed / Likely / Speculative. Speculative claims are framed as such on screen.
- Quote numbers with their date and unit.

## 10. Monetization-policy guardrails
- Original work only: no repetitive or mass-produced content, no template videos
  that differ only in a few words, no reuploads of others' material.
- Each video adds real commentary, explanation or analysis.
- Label realistic AI visuals on screen or in the description, and tick YouTube's
  "altered or synthetic content" disclosure when it applies.
- Credit every real image, clip and piece of music with its licence.
- Titles, thumbnails and tags describe only what is in the video.

